                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a nice idea for a game because you're tasked with growing a tree from a sapling and carefully pruning the branches to encourage it to grow in a very specific way, literally just the art of bonsai.\n\nThat said, while the idea is nice this game is incredibly unstable. Once your tree starts to really grow in size the game starts to chug big time. Even setting the game at a max FPS of 10 (that's the only video setting) doesn't help the fact that this game is put together really inefficiently. It's a massive resource hog and while I don't have a super duper top of the line gaming PC this game came out in 2016 and the parts in my tower are only a few years old yet this thing was making my fans scream and GPU get real hot for some reason.\n\nIt also crashes. Constantly. All the time, to the point where you'll find yourself clicking back to the menu to save your progress before you prune any branches because you never know if the one you click on will be the one that overloads this already beleaguered program. \n\nLike I said it's almost good, but even for a dollar this thing just runs so poorly and crashes so often that it's not fun to play.",
